170
00:11:50,800 --> 00:11:58,280
Now, one of the most common transformations that sites do is they exclude the entire query

171
00:11:58,280 --> 00:12:02,320
string from the cache key.

172
00:12:02,320 --> 00:12:09,040
And I'm definitely not the first person to notice this happening but this is massively underappreciated.

173
00:12:09,040 --> 00:12:15,760
And you might be wondering why because you would expect such a major transformation to be really

174
00:12:15,760 --> 00:12:22,800
obvious but actually it's incredibly easy to miss because the effect of this is that it disguises

175
00:12:22,800 --> 00:12:25,520
